A||N||5||jamesxnj||Question about high idle/clutch trouble||||5||
Z||000000||jamesxnj||07-21-2001||08:11 PM||||Hi I just bought an 85 gt 2.8  4 speed,86k miles.A spur of the momnet deal,In pretty good shape,The engine sounds strong,but the idle revs past 4k and will not settle down,the throttle seems to be OK,also it is almost impossible to get into any gears when the engine is running.Are these things possibly related? The gears can all be gotten into when the engine is off.I am thinking slave clynder,but there is tension in the clutch pedal.My 88 gt lost that sometimes before it went out entirely.I would really appreciate any of your thoughts ,suggestions before I take it to a  mechanic,I would like to be a little prepared for the worst case scenarios.I had 5 minutes to make an offer on the car as the seller was moving,and he took it..Thanks for reading.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||07-21-2001||09:14 PM||||Check the idle air control valve.<BR>Difficulty with gears may be High RPM related.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick86GT||07-21-2001||09:29 PM||||are you getting any codes? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||jamesxnj||07-22-2001||02:19 PM||||thanks Indiana and Patrick no I have not tried to get any codes,I am really mechanically challenged.about the most work I've done myself was replacing the headlights on my 88. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||LarryB||07-22-2001||03:35 PM||||Unplug the harness from the IAC valve and see if the idle changes.  If it doesn't, there's a good chance you've got a bad IAC, although there's a slim chance you've got a problem with the harness either at the IAC or into the ECM, or with the ECM itself. <P>If you don't have a Haynes or Chilton's manual you might want to take a quick trip to your auto parts store and pick one up.  In the meantime if you do a forum search you'll find out how to check the computer for codes, I wouldn't be surprised if you found code 35's.  All you need is a large paper clip and a T-15 Torx screwdriver.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||jamesxnj||07-22-2001||04:32 PM||||Thanks LarryB and all I appreciate the help!||||reg||1
